  "id": "COMPOUND:31601 - PROTEIN:5677",
  "verbalization": "Arundinol B appears to have a shared target, SNU-387, with multiple compounds, suggesting a potential role in modulating the activity of this molecule. The evidence indicates that SNU-387 is a target of several compounds, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, S-ethylcysteine zwitterion, and 2-(2,6-Dihydroxyphenyl)-5-hydroxy-3,6,7-trimethoxychromen-4-one, all of which ultimately target JM1. This suggests a possible pathway where Arundinol B may influence SNU-387's activity, which in turn affects JM1. The consistent targeting of SNU-387 by multiple compounds, coupled with the direct targeting of JM1 by these molecules, implies a potential mechanism by which Arundinol B could interact with JM1 through SNU-387. The evidence supports a functional link between Arundinol B and JM1, mediated through SNU-387, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated.",
